{"seq":4,"gate":"premortem","ts":"2026-09-07T02:40:17.178Z","ticket":"T288","data":{"promptOnly":true,"usageStatus":"unreported","verdict":"{\n  \"ticket\": \"T288\",\n  \"phase\": \"P1\",\n  \"verdict\": \"executable\",\n  \"review\": \"/tmp/loam-t278-evidence/T288-local-events-p1-review.md\",\n  \"unansweredQuestions\": [],\n  \"requiredContractCorrections\": [],\n  \"causes\": [\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"The new local-event module imports node:crypto for opening nonces, breaking the shipped browser Gateway bundle.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"The earlier candidate mandated node:crypto.randomBytes in the shared browser Gateway graph. The current matching JSON/spec now explicitly mandates portable getRandomValues instead.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Use the now-specified globalThis.crypto.getRandomValues on 32 bytes and lowercase hex; run the existing browser bundle suite/build. The contract correction is confirmed.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"None: portable randomness is now explicitly specified.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"A preplanted unknown-target negation suppresses a later local marked erasure tombstone through unchanged shared survivingTombstones logic, allowing failed-purge event bytes to regain meaning or making retry/replica standing disagree with the projector.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"erase.ts:204 applies lawfulNegated to every tombstone; generic ingress may already hold the negation before its protected target exists.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Apply the already specified no-protected-forgiveness rule in shared tombstone readers and projector: valid marked local erasure remains effective, generic preplants stay inert, ordinary unmarked forgiveness is unchanged. Test preplant, retaining purge, retry, replica and reopen.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"None: required by the candidate's explicit rule that unknown controls cannot later acquire protected meaning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"A same-key caller forges a marked event erasure through eraseReplica, or legitimate fan-out is incorrectly routed through generic federation and always refuses.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"Existing eraseReplica validates authorship then calls gw.federate; the new reserved local-control context requires provenance beyond signature and is excluded by generic federation.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Require the exact validated signed marked tombstone already held by the attached host authority and use the narrow internal validated erasure persistence seam. Test unattached forged calls, legitimate attached fan-out and classification after event purge.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"None: the revised candidate already specifies this trust boundary.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"The service records preselected offer IDs even when actual ingest rejected one, converting stored or offered bytes into false receive evidence.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"ingest.ts:521-533 persists the selected batch before ingestVia and currently counts only accepted outcomes; pooled presence alone cannot prove actual admitted receive.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Implement the revised admittedIds contract from accepted or independently confirmed identical held outcomes, excluding explicit rejection; exceptional ingest yields no successful attestation result. Use literal accepted, held, rejected and throwing fixtures.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"None: the revised actual-ingest and ids-option semantics are executable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"cause\": \"A stale failed pull overwrites a reopened channel or drop deadlocks waiting for scheduler.stop while a sync waits for the channel queue.\",\n      \"earliest_signal\": \"Current sync stamps debt and failure from pre-pull state; keepSyncing.stop awaits its running tick, which awaits channel.sync.\",\n      \"prevention\": \"Use the specified public queued/private in-commit split, queue every post-pull write, reject stale success/failure without writes, and never wait for scheduler.stop while holding commit. Test stale rejected pull, two handles, failed-drop retry and queue progress.\",\n      \"interrogation_question\": \"None: the final normative queue rules already settle the required behavior.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"testsRun\": [],\n  \"gateEvidenceRecorded\": false,\n  \"p5Approval\": false,\n  \"repositoryMutated\": false\n}","specPath":"/tmp/loam-t278-evidence/T288-spec.md"},"files":{"/tmp/loam-t278-evidence/T288-spec.md":"7adbd3d54576725c6ae7e49a09a3b361e0d74c56947d92c7992850c17760ba9e"},"prev":"a86428ed2a752afdd6c47b60892ef916ab289bb79127f19203909bc820e526a5","sig":"e5d8c3593a8f1b369bcc256aedfcdbd50be1ec10d05da07da0103dab7199758d"}
